From: Runeon Contributors <dev@runeon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: wake and free the msync waiters left on an index
 when its last reference goes

A downstream msync fix, not a WineHQ backport: WineHQ has no msync.
Runs only when WINEMSYNC is set.

A thread killed while it waits (by TerminateThread() or when its
process exits) never sends the unregister message, so its node stays
on every object it waited on. A thread's alert object is referenced
only by the server's thread object, not by a client, so once that
thread object goes the index drops to refcount 0 and is reused by the
next object created, with the dead thread's node still on its list.
The node then leaked, or woke whichever thread had reused that thread
id when the new object was signalled.

When destroy_all takes an index to refcount 0, run signal_all_internal()
on it: every node left is woken and returned to the pool. A live waiter
cannot be on that list, since it holds a reference for the duration of
its wait, but waking keeps it from hanging if one ever is; a woken
thread rechecks its objects, as after any wake. Nodes on objects that
a dead process still references are not covered: their refcount never
reaches 0.

--- a/server/msync.c
+++ b/server/msync.c
@@ -391,7 +391,16 @@
 
     refcount = __atomic_sub_fetch( &obj->refcount, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
 
-    if (!refcount) last_destroyed_idx = shm_idx;
+    if (!refcount)
+    {
+        /* A thread killed while waiting never unregisters, and a thread's alert
+         * object holds no client reference, so the list can still hold nodes
+         * when the last reference goes. Drain it now: waits on the next object
+         * at this index are registered on this thread after this message.
+         * Waking instead of only freeing keeps a live waiter from hanging. */
+        signal_all_internal( shm_idx );
+        last_destroyed_idx = shm_idx;
+    }
 }
 
